# Dev Team Orchestrator routing

When the user asks for team/feature work via **zteam**, **@zteam**, **/zteam**, or **dev-team-orchestrator** (requirements, tech design, implementation plan, tests, or a full pipeline):

1. **Before the pipeline:** call MCP `get_zteam_config` with `workspaceRoot` (+ `projectRoot`). If `needsConfig`, do **not** call `run_development_pipeline` — run `@zteam/models` / `@zteam/config` first.
2. Call the MCP tool `run_development_pipeline` on **`user-zteam`** (MCP server key `zteam`).
3. **Dual runtime:** if `llmRuntime=ninerouter`, do **not** use Cursor `Task` for team roles — MCP drives 9router. If `llmRuntime=cursor`, MCP returns `delegationPlaybook` — run stages via Cursor Task in order (do **not** also call 9router). Never mix families in one config.
4. Cursor Task subagents use Cursor models and **never** hit 9router (cursor path only).

Prefer the project skill **`zteam`** (`/zteam` or `@zteam`) for the short trigger; this rule still applies when the user uses the long name.

## Spec-driven pipeline

The MCP tool runs LangGraph. **Always pass `workspaceRoot`** = absolute path of the Cursor-open folder (skill contract). Optional `projectRoot` (default `"."`) is resolved under that workspace. Prefer `projectRoot` like `samples/my-app` so the MCP package README is not overwritten. Writes into the orchestrator package root with `projectRoot: "."` are rejected.

**Subcommands (skill):** `@zteam/config` (full setup), `@zteam/models` (LLM ids → `.zteam/config.json`), `@zteam/documentation` (`workflow=docs`), `@zteam/tests` (`workflow=tests` + `slug`). See [`.zteam/README.MD`](../../.zteam/README.MD).

Team models: `.zteam/config.json` (app → workspace → env `MODEL_*` → defaults). Config gate opens if a config file exists **or** explicit `MODEL_*` env is set (`configGateSatisfied`). Otherwise `failureKind=needsConfig` — use `@zteam/models` / `@zteam/config` / `get_zteam_config` / `write_zteam_config`. Prefer **not** setting sticky `WORKSPACE_ROOT` in `mcp.json`.

**Requirements (full/docs):** iterative — bootstrap Resume + Pré Requirements → SA expands one pré-req at a time → clean README → UI/UX juice addendum (score ≥7) → fidelity → TA → UI/UX look-and-feel (`.docs/ui-ux.md`) → SA todo plan → per-slug SA→UI/UX→TA specs (+ architecture critic) → (scaffold → **QA TDD red** → **SE TDD green** → delivery critic → **QA TDD verify** / `markTodoDone` if not docs-only).

| Stage | Env var | Default | Writes / reads |
|---|---|---|---|
| System Architect (requirements) | `MODEL_SYSTEM_ARCHITECT` | `9RSA-system-architect-free` | bootstrap `README.md` → per-item `.docs/requirements.md` → clean README |
| Fidelity critic | (heurística) | — | FAIL hard vs `userIdea` (redo SA); no silent pass on stub/API drift |
| Technology Architect | `MODEL_TECHNOLOGY_ARCHITECT` | `9RTA-technology-architect-free` | `.docs/technologies.md` + README update |
| System Architect (specs) | `MODEL_SYSTEM_ARCHITECT` | same | `.docs/todo.md` + `.docs/specs/*.spec.md` + README |
| Delivery critic (architecture) | (heurística) | — | gaps idea ↔ tech/specs; may reopen TA |
| Scaffold | (no LLM) | — | vite+vitest template / augment missing shell files |
| QA TDD red | `MODEL_QA_ENGINEER` | `9RQA-qa-free` | Failing tests from specs (use cases / screen-flow); **does not** mark `[x]` |
| Software Engineer | `MODEL_SOFTWARE_ENGINEER` | `9RSE-software-engineer-free` | TDD green; Clean Code + `===SELF_CHECK===`; `verifyDelivery` + `tsc`; redo with `deliveryFixRound`; **does not** `markTodoDone` |
| Delivery critic (delivery) | (heurística) | — | reopen incomplete slugs after SE |
| QA TDD verify | `MODEL_QA_ENGINEER` | same | Run suite + gaps; **`markTodoDone` when tests pass**; optional `===TECH_DEBT===` → `.docs/tech-debt.md`; bootstrapFix vs SE fix by error class |
| System Architect (post-dev) | `MODEL_SYSTEM_ARCHITECT` | same | Summary from requirements+README → `.docs/user-report.md`; if tech debt: judge vs spirit, update docs if necessary, plan-mode `.docs/tech-debt-plan.md` for user decision |
| Orchestrator finalize | (no LLM) | — | README status + `.docs/pipeline-result.json` (metrics: retries, `llmEmpty`, `userReport`, …) |

**Empty LLM:** no silent charter/TBD/`implement-core` stubs — `failureKind=llm_empty`. Classified failures include `spec_incomplete`, `tsc`, `bootstrap`, `fidelity`, `qa`, `healthcheck`.

**Docs-only:** pass `workflow: "docs"` (or deprecated `docsOnly: true` / CLI `--docs-only` / `--workflow=docs`).

**Workflows:** omit `workflow` for auto-routing, or set `full` | `docs` | `feature` | `punch` | `fix` | `resume` | `tests` | `analyze`. Optional `slug` (feature/tests), `role` + `scope` (analyze). See [`src/workflows/`](../../src/workflows/). Resume reopens phantom `[x]` todos whose Files to touch are missing on disk.

**CLI:** `npm run pipeline -- --workflow punch --project-root samples/foo "idea…"` and `pipeline:docs` / `pipeline:resume`.

**Graph viz:** `npm run graph` prints Mermaid and writes `.docs/langgraph.mmd`. Mid-failure: prefer `workflow=resume` (not copying sibling projects).

```text
❌ BAD (ninerouter):  Task(subagent_type="qa-engineer") instead of MCP
✅ GOOD (ninerouter): CallDynamicTool(user-zteam.run_development_pipeline)
✅ GOOD (cursor):     run_development_pipeline → execute delegationPlaybook via Task in order (QA-red → SE → delivery critic → QA-verify)
```

Exception: editing **this** MCP server's own source (e.g. `src/orchestrator.ts`) may use normal tools; still prefer not to fake team roles via Task when the user expected a 9router pipeline run.
